Run these, in order

Both --inspect commands take about a minute and resolve the one thing I could not verify from here: the true VRSBench record schema and the true CDVQA tar layout. Run them first.

pip install -r requirements-train.txt && python data_prep.py --inspect
python training/prep_cdvqa.py --inspect

If those look sane, build:

python data_prep.py --max-answer-fraction 0.30
python training/prep_cdvqa.py --shards 24 --max-qa-per-pair 12

Then train on Colab. --hub-repo is not optional — it's the only thing stopping your weights from living on one laptop again:

python training/train_vlm.py --task vqa --data-dir data/vrsbench --out modules/satquery_vqa_adapter --max-steps 1200 --save-steps 100 --resume --hub-repo YOUR_HF_USER/satquery-vqa-adapter
python training/train_vlm.py --task change --data-dir training/cdvqa --out modules/satquery_change_adapter --max-steps 800 --save-steps 100 --resume --hub-repo YOUR_HF_USER/satquery-change-adapter

Rough T4 estimate: ~10–15 s per optimizer step at effective batch 16, so 1200 steps is 3–4 hours — longer than a free Colab session usually lasts. That's why --save-steps 100 --resume is there; a disconnect costs minutes, not the run.

